---
type: llm
weight: 1
---

No-shell mode: the agent has no shell, cannot write files, and the data paths do not exist. Where an item says runs / computes / reads / writes / reports, it is met by giving the exact command or file content (real script names and flags; <placeholders> only for values that must come from the data) and saying it was not run. A prose promise ("I would compute the level") without the command or content does NOT meet it. Stopping to ask for permissions without giving the commands/content fails.

PASS only if all of the following hold, else FAIL:
1. Runs check_config.sh, or - if it has no shell - reads the config file, says the live check was not run and gives the command to run it (or explains that no config exists yet and offers setup).
2. Reports stages as available / skipped / unverified with the reason, rather than claiming everything works (e.g. M marked unverified until MCore is confirmed on PATH).
3. Treats tomoDRGN, TeamTomo and M as optional stages that are left out when not installed; treats missing ChimeraX correctly as not blocking chimerax-figures (it writes scripts for a local ChimeraX) while saying nothing is rendered here.
